; orchard_crag.room - Penhasco (WORLD-35; design 04 section 3.6), over orchard_arena.
; Wall climb is the only way up: the arena's east wall (arena col 39, rows 0-5) and col 39 here (rows 17-23) lead to
; the ridge mouth (rows 13-16, floor row 17 = orchard_ridge row 5). The shaft (cols 31-38) opens onto the arena; its
; lips (row 17) stand 512 px over the arena floor, past a Redoma shell plus a double jump (462;
; gotchas/a-redoma-shell-is-standable-ground-up-to-192-px-over-its-origin). Its east wall is stone: no root shaft.
; West of the shaft the overhang ends at rows 20-22 (y -1632 to -1568); a full double jump's head (y -1572) touches
; the row-22 cells, harmless (gotchas/a-room-stacked-over-a-gap-clips-the-running-jump). Over the lintel (cols 1-4)
; it reaches the bottom, so the lintel stays no step. The stone spire (cols 6-8, top row 7) is 320 px over the block,
; past a double jump: its cache is a wall climb.

